  "content": [
    {
      "text": "shall a man leave his father and his mother, Gen. 2:24 (Moses 3:24; Abr. 5:18). Eve; because she was the mother of all living, Gen. 3:20 (Moses 4:26). she shall be a mother of nations, Gen. 17:16. Rebekah … be thou the mother of thousands, Gen. 24:60. Honour thy father and thy mother, Ex. 20:12 (Deut. 5:16; Matt. 15:4; Mark 7:10; Eph. 6:2; 1 Ne. 17:55; Mosiah 13:20). I Deborah arose … I arose a mother in Israel, Judg. 5:7. his mother made him a little coat, 1 Sam. 2:19. He maketh the barren woman … to be a joyful mother of children, Ps. 113:9. forsake not the law of thy mother, Prov. 1:8. a foolish son is the heaviness of his mother, Prov. 10:1. a foolish man despiseth his mother, Prov. 15:20. despise not thy mother when she is old, Prov. 23:22. child left to himself bringeth his mother to shame, Prov. 29:15. their queens thy nursing mothers, Isa. 49:23 (1 Ne. 21:23; 2 Ne. 6:7; 10:9). for your transgressions is your mother put away, Isa. 50:1 (2 Ne. 7:1). As is the mother, so is her daughter, Ezek. 16:44. daughter riseth up against her mother, Micah 7:6 (Matt. 10:35; Luke 12:53).",
